Spec: Shared kernel

Purpose:
  Cross-cutting pieces used by every feature package: the single SQLite connection and the shared page shell. It
  holds no domain rules and no routes.

Owns:
  ./db.py
  ./layout.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Must:
  ./db.py opens the `fastlite` `Database` at `/data/app.db`, creating the parent directory when it does not exist,
  and exposes the single connection that every feature's repository_sqlite.py imports.
  ./layout.py renders the shared page shell: header, the Tailwind Play CDN script tag and the HTMX script tag, used
  by every feature's view.py.
  ./layout.py's header renders a horizontal top-bar nav linking the Semester view (`/`) and the Realization view
  (`/realizations`), highlighting whichever one the calling route registers as active, and a slot for that page's
  own selector control (for example a Semester or CourseRealization dropdown); it takes the active link name and the
  already-rendered selector as plain arguments so it still needs no feature imports.
  ./layout.py's header also takes an already-rendered login/logout link as a plain argument, per
  ../auth/auth.sdd, so it still needs no import of ../auth/auth.sdd's services.py or routes.py.

Must not:
  ./db.py and ./layout.py must not import any feature package's domain.py, ports.py, services.py,
  repository_sqlite.py, view.py or routes.py.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement ./layout.py with the shared page shell (header plus the Tailwind Play CDN and HTMX headers) for the
    first hardcoded semester-view pass
  [x] Extend ./layout.py's header with the horizontal top-bar nav between the Semester and Realization views and a
    slot for each view's own selector dropdown
  [x] Implement ./db.py: the shared `fastlite` `Database` connection at `/data/app.db`, now that real persistence
    begins
